Package: homelab-prometheus
Architecture: all
Depends: perl (>= 5.36),
         prometheus,
         homelab-common,
         libyaml-libyaml-perl,
         libmojolicious-perl
Recommends: homelab-agent, homelab-grafana
Description: Prometheus monitoring host for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Turns a host into the fleet's Prometheus monitoring server. Depends on
 the Ubuntu-archive prometheus package and points it (via a
 prometheus.service drop-in) at a config whose scrape targets are file_sd
 files regenerated from the LIVE fleet -- homelab-prometheus-pull reads
 homelab-api's feature-backends view (the same pull model as
 homelab-haproxy/homelab-webproxy) on a timer, so Prometheus always
 scrapes exactly the hosts currently advertising each exporter. Ships an
 nftables drop-in opening just the egress this host needs (homelab-api +
 the fleet exporter ports) and advertises itself into the fleet topology.
 Pair with homelab-node-exporter fleet-wide (host metrics) and
 homelab-grafana (dashboards) on the same host.
